TIMES(2)                       P32W Unix                        TIMES(2)

NAME
       times - get process times

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/times.h>

       long times(struct tms *buf);

              struct tms {
                  unsigned tms_utime;   /* user time */
                  unsigned tms_stime;   /* system time */
                  unsigned tms_cutime;  /* children's user time */
                  unsigned tms_cstime;  /* children's system time */
              };

DESCRIPTION
       times stores in *buf the CPU time used so far by the calling
       process, in user mode and in the kernel, and the same for
       all of its children that have terminated and been waited
       for (and their waited-for children in turn). The unit is
       the clock tick: CLK_TCK (50) a second. Each tick is charged
       to whichever process it interrupted. buf may be a null
       pointer.

RETURN VALUE
       The number of clock ticks since the system started; -1 on
       an error, with errno set.

ERRORS
       EFAULT  buf is a bad address.

SEE ALSO
       time(1), time(2), wait(2), fork(2)

BUGS
       Times are sampled, not measured: a process that runs for
       less than a tick at a time may be charged nothing, or too
       much.
